(136719, 6766, 3080, '<td valign="top">I guess I don''t get the title, but that''s ok, cause as long as I get the photo, that''s what counts, right?  Definately trash related, and there s definately something going on in the shot.  Not JUST a photo of garbage.  The angle and framing/cropping are good.  Lighting is nice for the shot as well.  I like the overall feel of this photo.  Good luck in the challenge. ~hbunch7187~</td>', 'I guess I don''t get the title, but that''s ok, cause as long as I get the photo, that''s what counts, right?  Definately trash related, and there s definately something going on in the shot.  Not JUST a photo of garbage.  The angle and framing/cropping are good.  Lighting is nice for the shot as well.  I like the overall feel of this photo.  Good luck in the challenge. ~hbunch7187~', '2002-10-13 20:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(136720, 6766, 1037, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure where this is from, but I''ve seen many scenes like this on TV and always felt like they make the most poignant statement about the poverty and inequality in the world... the poor fossicking through the things the wealthy discard just to get by. The depth of feeling in your photo is astonishing. 10 - lisae</td>', 'I''m not sure where this is from, but I''ve seen many scenes like this on TV and always felt like they make the most poignant statement about the poverty and inequality in the world... the poor fossicking through the things the wealthy discard just to get by. The depth of feeling in your photo is astonishing. 10 - lisae', '2002-10-13 22:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
