(135771, 6689, 2221, '<td valign="top">Maybe you should have taken this photo from the other side. I learned that when viewing a photo the eyes follow along the lines (if there are any). In your case the eyes want to wander to the left because of the perspective lines in the fence. When shooting from the other direction these lines would converge in direction to the can and thus attracting to eyes to your subject. Just an idea. -stephan<br/></td>', 'Maybe you should have taken this photo from the other side. I learned that when viewing a photo the eyes follow along the lines (if there are any). In your case the eyes want to wander to the left because of the perspective lines in the fence. When shooting from the other direction these lines would converge in direction to the can and thus attracting to eyes to your subject. Just an idea. -stephan', '2002-10-13 09:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
