(136570, 6754, 2586, '<td valign="top">This was a spoof on the Zen and The Art of Motorcycle Repair book. To underscore the garbage/recycle theme I set it up on top of the recycle bin, turned upside down.  In my mind, there''s something zen-like to those two simple, clean empty cans as opposed to tons of filthy garbage overflowing a trashcan or a  dumpster. The essence of zen is not about practicing meditation endless hours a day but perhaps to work with it in your everyday living. So, I try to exercise restraint in the amount of garbage I generate. This picture was an attempt to reflect something, just a little something,  of myself in a very uninteresting challenge about garbage.</td>', 'This was a spoof on the Zen and The Art of Motorcycle Repair book. To underscore the garbage/recycle theme I set it up on top of the recycle bin, turned upside down.  In my mind, there''s something zen-like to those two simple, clean empty cans as opposed to tons of filthy garbage overflowing a trashcan or a  dumpster. The essence of zen is not about practicing meditation endless hours a day but perhaps to work with it in your everyday living. So, I try to exercise restraint in the amount of garbage I generate. This picture was an attempt to reflect something, just a little something,  of myself in a very uninteresting challenge about garbage.', '2002-10-18 16:04:00.000000', NULL, 0),
